Privacy Policy – Hide Paid YouTube Videos
Last updated: 20 October 2026

Hide Paid YouTube Videos is a browser extension that removes paywalled videos (members-only videos, movies to buy or rent, and other paid content) from YouTube.

What the extension handles
- YouTube page content: on youtube.com, the extension reads video links on the page and requests each video's YouTube page to check whether it is behind a paywall.
- A local cache: the IDs of videos it has checked, whether each one is paid (and which kind), and the day each free one was checked.
- Your settings: whether the filter is on, and which kinds of paid videos to hide (members-only, paid movies & shows).

Where it is stored
All of this is stored only in your browser, using Chrome's local extension storage. It is never sent to the developer or to any third party. The only network requests the extension makes are to youtube.com.

What is not collected
The extension does not collect personal information, does not use analytics or advertising, and does not sell or share any data.

Your control
The "Clear saved results" button in the extension's popup clears the cache. Removing the extension deletes everything it stored.

